DEVIATION FROM BYTE-FOR-BYTE VENDORING, applied to code/legume/.

This is the only vendored tree in the benchmark that differs from its pin.
It is deliberate and was decided by the codebase owner; it is isolated in one
commit so that `git show` on that commit is exactly the deviation.

WHAT   Four in-place accumulations rewritten out-of-place, at three files:
         legume/gme/gme.py:1720   rad_c['te'][clad_ind] += ...
         legume/gme/gme.py:1743   rad_c['tm'][clad_ind] += ...
         legume/utils.py:28       ftinv += ...
         legume/phc/layer.py:175  FT[ind0] += bd.abs(Vmax)

WHY    Each accumulator is allocated as a plain numpy array (bd.zeros or
       np.zeros). Under the autograd backend the right-hand side is an
       autograd ArrayBox, and `ndarray += ArrayBox` makes numpy return
       NotImplemented, raising TypeError. Assigning out-of-place lets the box
       propagate. The first two sites break every differentiated run with
       compute_im=True, which is the default; the third breaks differentiation
       through get_field_xy, the real-space field reconstruction.

SINCE  Upstream commit d663dd5 (2020-03-12) for the gme.py sites; present in
       every tag from 0.1.2 through v1.0.3. No tagged release has ever had a
       working gradient-of-Q path.

SAFE   For a plain numpy array `a = a + b` and `a += b` compute identical
       values; only allocation differs. Measured, not assumed: on the numpy
       backend, freqs, freqs_im and a reconstructed real-space field are
       sha256-identical between the pristine and patched trees. The third
       site is exercised by that field comparison. The fourth site's two
       formulations are bit-identical on plain arrays when its branch fires,
       checked over random trials (maxdiff 0.0), and differentiating geometry
       with the branch NOT taken returns 9.25608383 on both trees.

EFFECT tests/test_gme_grad.py: TypeError -> pass; whole suite 12 passed +
       1 failed -> 13 passed. Example notebook 08: TypeError -> passes in
       161 s. Example notebook 06: gets past the defect and runs its real
       10-epoch Adam cavity optimization, then exceeds the 300 s per-cell cap
       used here; the cap, not a defect, is what stops it. Gradient of the sum
       of Q factors now returns in one reverse-mode pass and agrees with finite
       differences to 2.7e-02, inside upstream's own 1e-1 test bound.

FOURTH legume/phc/layer.py:175, in Layer.compute_exc_ft (the exciton
SITE   potential transform), is guarded by `if FT[ind0][0] < 0`. No test or
       example takes that branch: test_polariton reaches the guard but reads
       FT[ind0][0] == 0.0, so the line never runs upstream. It is nonetheless
       a real defect, reproduced by differentiating a shape radius with a
       negative Vmax: pristine raises TypeError ("only integer scalar arrays
       can be converted to a scalar index"), patched returns 5.48617265, which
       agrees with a central difference to 1.9e-11. Fixed with bd.where rather
       than an index-assignment so it dispatches on both backends.

SEARCH A static scan for `X = zeros(...)` followed by `X +=` found these sites
       plus six in legume/primitives.py that are correct (a vjp body receives
       concrete arrays, never boxes, and test_primitives passes). That scan is
       a heuristic: it did not catch the two gme.py sites, whose accumulator is
       built by a dict comprehension, so the class may have further members on
       paths nothing executes.

